; Handler for "talk to": the character takes some of the orders
;
; The default handler (VerbHandlers) of command 53, "talk to". The parser has
; already stored the orders typed after the name in order slots (#R$7EBA); this
; decides how many of them the addressed character (FirstObject) obeys and
; calls ClaimOrderSlots with that number.
; .
; A character with no NPC record obeys none. After a character has spoken to the
; player (ReplyGiven is set by #R$A8D2) the reply is accepted: one order. Otherwise
; the NPC record's byte +6 is its obedience: 0 obeys none, any other value n
; obeys a random number of orders from 0 to n; when that comes out as 0 the
; character says "<obj1> says "No"".
; .
; Only a real performance counts (CommitOrAbort drops out when the command is
; only being tried).
;
; FirstObject The character spoken to
@label=TalkToCharacter
c$9034 CALL $9D44    ; abandon unless performing
 $9037 LD A,($B6E8)  ; the character
 $903A CALL $9A85    ; its NPC record in IY
@isub=CP END_MARK
 $903D CP $FF        ; no record?
 $903F LD A,$00      ; (keeps the flags) no orders
 $9041 JR Z,$9058    ;
 $9043 LD A,($B6F9)  ; ReplyGiven: 1 order when it just spoke
 $9046 CP $00        ;
 $9048 JR NZ,$9058   ;
 $904A LD A,(IY+$06) ; obedience
 $904D CP $00        ;
 $904F JR Z,$9058    ; none: no orders
 $9051 CALL $9C9F    ; random number of orders 0 to obedience
 $9054 CP $00        ;
 $9056 JR Z,$905C    ; 0: refuse
*$9058 CALL $7EBA    ; ClaimOrderSlots: keep A orders
 $905B RET           ;
*$905C LD HL,$B1E3   ; "<obj1> says "No""
 $905F CALL $72DD    ;
 $9062 SUB A         ; no orders
 $9063 JR $9058      ;
